## ✍️ Phase 4: Copy Generation & Recommendation Framework

### 4.1 Core Copy Generation Workflows


┌─────────────────────────┐     ┌───────────────────────────┐     ┌───────────────────────────┐
│  Uncovered Motivation   │ ──> │   Adapt Structure of      │ ──> │  Persona-Specific Variant │
│  or VoC Trigger Moment  │     │   Proven Winning Copy     │     │  (Tailored Noun / Hook)   │
└─────────────────────────┘     └───────────────────────────┘     └───────────────────────────┘

* **Structure Adaptation:** Apply the sentence structure and rhythm of historical winning ads to newly identified persona motivations.
* **Benefit Stacking:** Combine complementary single-benefit claims into multi-benefit messaging variations when data indicates stacking increases conversion density.
* **Implied vs. Stated Testing:** Draft paired assets that compare explicit claims against implicit, story-driven demonstrations of the same benefit.

### 4.2 Standardized Output Schema

| Copy Text | Placement / Format | Persona Target | Priority | Provenance / Origin | Test Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| *"Sample Headline"* | Primary Text / Search Headline | Core Persona A | P1 | Iteration on Proven Winner | Draft |
| *"Sample Headline"* | Landing Page Hero H1 | Expansion Persona B | P2 | VoC Review Analysis | Backlog |

